00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.000 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  under the shadow of the mighty world  tree egg drasil three factions battled  for supremacy in a strange and hostile  new land this is the world of rend an  innovative team-based survival game set  in the apocalyptic aftermath of Ragnarok  rend is the first game from frost cube  studios an indie developer comprised of  talents who can list World of Warcraft  overwatch League of Legends and wildstar  on their collective resume their mission  is to create a survival game that not  only inspires cooperation and creativity  but is also quite simply fun to play  here are five ways that Rend  distinguishes itself from the survival  pack number one there's no I in survival  well apart from the first one obviously  when you join a server you must first  choose to align yourself with one of  three rival factions Conclave order or  revenant each faction supports a maximum  of twenty players  meaning you could roam the diverse  biomes of a ravaged Midgard in the  company of 59 other players everybody's  in the same boat to begin with you have  no clothes no supplies and no shelter  and in a game where hunger thirst and  even temperature are a constant threat  to your well-being it's imperative that  you immediately scavenge enough raw  materials to dress armed and feed  yourself once you're self-sufficient you  can start to work towards the greater  good each faction has a base which is  protected by a shield while most of the  time anyway more on that later  everyone's efforts be that gathering  crafting hunting fighting or gaining  insight into the environments feed into  the entire tribes resources and  knowledge allowing you to grow your base  and your collective skill set rend is  not a game for the selfish yes you'll  always need to keep one eye on your  various metres to ensure you don't drop  dead from starvation exposure or a  massive wolf bite but your real focus  should be on making like a doomsday  prepper and stockpiling for the war  ahead because number two war is coming  rend is at once a pvp and PVE experience  in the process of shattering Midgard  Ragnarok has also angered a  lot of the local wildlife and so the  further you stray from the safety of  your bass the more likely it is you'll  run into hostile beasts in search of  fast food as such arming yourself is  critical to avoiding an embarrassing  walk of shame back to your lost gear  then of course there's the matter of up  to 40 other player-controlled warriors  wandering the land doing their utmost to  ensure their faction superiority run  into a rival and there's really only one  option fight  despite the ancient mythological setting  wrens combat is range focused offering  an array of craftable bows that evoke  classic firearm archetypes your standard  short bow is wrens equivalent of a rifle  a single shot weapon that works best at  range crossbows our first style assault  rifles repeaters are SMGs and so on  knowing your way around a weapon is  vital not just for these accidental  encounters but for a couple of  game-changing features that could turn  the tide in favor of your faction first  up there's control points these ancient  relics are dotted around various  strategic points on the map and once  captured will grant your faction all  manner of tactical bonuses including xp  loot and artifacts items artifacts are  one-of-a-kind weapons and equipment that  endow you with superhuman abilities as  you can imagine this makes control  points highly desirable and hence are  likely to be a reason for rival factions  to group up and wrestle for Dominion but  these skirmishes are far from the war I  alluded to they're merely a prelude to  the reckoning remember how I said that  faction bases are protected by a shield  most of the time yep well the reckoning  accounts for the rest of that time twice  a week on the official servers the  shield's on olfaction bases come down  and a PvE war commences from the spirit  realm emerges hordes of the lost  dishonored warriors returned as mindless  monsters all in pursuit of your  destruction they'll march in  increasingly challenging waves doing  their damnedest to bring down your  factions harder and score and  potentially the entire faction with it  the lost are tougher than the beasts  you'll typically encounter so taking  them down requires preparation and  collaboration preparation comes in the  form of developing and constructing  automated turrets and reinforced walls  while collaboration means combining  offense with your faction mates to where  the loss down and earned plenty of XP  and faction score in the process should  you survive this assault there's  absolutely no room to breathe  all faction based shields will remain  inoperative and the PvE war makes way  for a PvP war leaving you with a big  decision to make do you hang back and  protect your devastated base from  further attack or do you mount a raid on  your rivals which brings me to point  three you can actually win and lose and  like other survival games Rend actually  has a win state one aspect I've  deliberately failed to mention so far is  that all this base building and inter  faction rivalry has a point  boiled down to its core rend is a race a  three-way contest to be the first to  gather enough spirits to earn the right  to ascend to Valhalla any spirits  gathered during your travels are  automatically deposited in the divinity  stone within your base as the divinity  stone is actually connected to incra  cells roots your progress can be tracked  as a glowing bar edged on to the trunk  of the world tree however the amounts of  spirits held can go up and down control  points play a huge part in keeping those  spirits coming as they not only generate  them but also deposit them directly to  your stone then of course there's the  aforementioned option to storm into a  rivals base and ruin all of their hard  work obviously the same can happen to  you and between a vicious assault by the  lost and human vultures come reckoning  day you could be facing losses that will  set your efforts back by days and that's  actual days not in-game ones but if  after potentially months of struggle  your faction reigns victorious you'll be  chosen to join the surviving gods in  Valhalla on a more practical level  you'll also be granted a greater number  of Ascension points which can be  exchanged for perks that persist across  all servers and future game cycles  number four it's a fascinating hybrid of  genres in order to address what some  perceives to be the less desirable  aspects of the survival genre rend  cherry-picks elements from mmo's MOBAs  and sandbox games the introduction of a  win-loss state is obviously a big one  but this influence is also evident  from the sheer breadth and depth of  crafting and character customization  options crafting is the first aspect  you'll encounter as it's essential for  gearing yourself up with the  fundamentals beyond rudimentary tools  basic clothing and simple weaponry  you'll discover an extensive array of  crafting categories most of which  contain items unavailable to you from  the get-go this is yet another example  of how Rend encourages collaboration in  order to grow your crafting options  you'll have to build and upgrade  crafting stations in your base and in  order to do that everyone needs to  donate the sparks of genius earned from  performing general actions to the bases  research obelisks in fact everything you  do in rend rewards you in some way for  every action you're able to perform  there's an Associated skill 15 in total  spread across three broad categories  adventuring crafting and combat these  can all be individually leveled up to a  maximum of 50 and award you a choice of  two perks each time he hits a key  milestone adding even greater  flexibility to your character  development is the archetype system your  character can permanently adopt two of  four available archetypes assassin  warlord Pathfinder and Shaymin and each  of those has its own talent tree full of  useful passive and active talents your  learn points to boost these talents as  your character levels up giving you  plenty of opportunity to tailor a  character that suits your style of play  number five you can ride a giant wolf or  as they're known in Rend prowl fangs  which is a much cooler name anyway most  of the creatures roaming wrens biomes  aren't only there to fill your inventory  with nourishing meats and useful pelts  for crafting they're also there to offer  you a sweet ride and back you up in  combat transforming a creature from a  snarling man-eating beast into your  snarling man-eating beasts isn't simple  sadly no you're gonna have to kill them  first seems impractical but in a game  where you can traverse between the realm  of the living and the spirit realm it's  quite possible to bring a freshly slain  creature back from the dead and under  your thrall once you've crafted the  means of entering the spirit realm  you'll have to do some serious  preparation the spirit realm itself  isn't a place for the corporeal so your  vitals will drain at an increasing rate  the longer you hang about then you've  got the matter of the lost roaming  around and as we've already established  they're not ones for small talk finally  you've got to do your research when it  comes to taming the Beast of your  choosing do they respond to a certain  type of food magic auras maybe perhaps  they need to be shot with spirit arrows  provided you figure out the best  approach and emerge relatively unscathed  congratulations you're the proud owner  of a freshly resurrected pet depending  on which of rennes diverse fauna you've  tamed you'll gain a welcome boost in a  number of departments some are born  fighters or great for hauling heavy  resources while others might make  harvesting a breeze or provide vital  muscle when laying siege to our control  points or base you can't ride on all of  them sadly but you can definitely ride a  giant wolf if you fancy yourself worthy  enough to survive against the odds  vanquish your enemies and earn your  rightful place among the gods rend is  exclusively available in early access on  Steam

